-- check/bad: the numbers-only hint must not name `<`, `>`, `<=` or `>=`.
-- `docs/design/static-dispatch-spike.md` §3.1 makes the four ordering
-- operators the receiver type's `compare`, so `"a" < "b"` compiles; a hint
-- that calls them numbers-only, or that offers `String.compare` as the only
-- way to order text, is now false. Both arms that carry the hint are here:
-- a `String` where an `Int` was wanted, and a `number` that met a `String`
-- THROUGH `<` itself — the operator pins both operands to one type (A.33),
-- which is the real mistake and has nothing to do with ordering.
pub count : Int
count =
    "12"


pub ordered : Bool
ordered =
    "a" < 1
